<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Bar appearance for API 27 and later.

  `android:windowLightNavigationBar` was introduced in API 27. It has to live in
  a versioned resource because the default theme is also read on API 23, where
  the attribute does not exist, and lint's NewApi check fails the build on it
  rather than on the runtime no-op.

  The parent is Theme.OcuBea.Base, NOT the Material theme. A versioned resource
  replaces the default one instead of merging with it, so declaring this style
  with its own Material parent meant the seven shared items, namely windowBackground,
  the bar colours and the primary colour, were simply absent on API 27 and later.
  See the aapt2 dump in values/styles.xml for the measurement that showed it.
  The earlier note in this file claimed the opposite, that declaring it
  separately was the safe choice; it was not, and the claim is what the size=1
  dump refutes.

  The value is false because this app is dark-only. A light navigation bar asks
  for dark icons, and that was the measured bug on a Redmi Note 12 Pro running
  Android 16: the bar painted RGB(255,255,255) over 98.6% of its area with icons
  that were light on white and unreadable.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.OcuBea" parent="Theme.OcuBea.Base">
        <item name="android:windowLightNavigationBar">false</item>
    </style>
</resources>